<%#
  THE ID LIST BEHIND A COUNT -- the filtered view's whole content, and the
  reason a count on the audit page is a LINK rather than a number.

  `rows` is `[id, record_url, gaps]` triples, where `gaps` is the ARRAY of gap
  keys that row fails (a job missing three fields is one row with three keys).
  The RECORD cell is the link -- there is no separate "open" button, because a
  second control for the same destination is a dead end dressed as an action.

  A row whose url is nil (a candidate whose job is gone has no record page to
  open) renders the bare id in a `.chip.miss` rather than a dead link -- the
  phase-1 convention for "absent, and that is intentional".

  Locals: rows (Array), empty (the sentence when there is nothing to list).
%>
<% if rows.empty? %>
  <p class="jev-note"><%= empty %></p>
<% else %>
  <div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table class="candidates">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Record</th>
          <th>Gaps</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% rows.each do |id, url, gaps| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <% if url %>
                <%= link_to "##{id}", url, class: "mono", title: "Open record #{id}" %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="chip miss mono">#<%= id %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td>
              <% Array(gaps).each do |gap_key| %>
                <span class="chip mono"><%= gap_key %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% end %>
